      Create the custom resource (CR) for the JobSet Operator:
      <ol>
      <li>Navigate to <strong>Installed Operators</strong> → <strong>JobSet Operator</strong>.</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Provided APIs</strong>, click <strong>Create instance</strong> in the <strong>JobSetOperator</strong> pane.</li>
      <li>Set the name to <strong>cluster</strong>.</li>
      <li>Set the <strong>managementState</strong> to <strong>Managed</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Create</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      </ol>
